  "articleBody": "While patching a minor nail hole in drywall is straightforward, garage walls face distinct demands that make certain repairs unsafe for quick fixes. If your garage shares walls or ceilings with your living areas, compromised drywall can expose your home to drafts, vehicle exhaust, and fire hazards.\n\nSigns It Is Time to Call a Professional:\n- Water stains or swelling near ceiling joints beneath upstairs bedrooms, indicating plumbing leaks or moisture accumulation in the floor assembly.\n- Cracks or gaping holes along the shared garage-to-house separation wall, which compromise the required fire barrier.\n- Soft, crumbling gypsum board caused by vehicle impact that also knocked internal wall framing or electrical boxes loose.\n- Mold growth or musty odors behind the wall cavity, which requires controlled removal and thorough cavity drying before closing.\n- Gaps around utility penetrations where pipes, vents, or wiring pass into the residence without proper fire-stopping seals.\n\nWhat to Do Next\nDo not simply skim joint compound over active moisture or compromised Type X assemblies. HH Remodeling LLC specializes in residential restoration, framing, drywall repair, and finish painting throughout the Denver area. Call Abraham Becerra at 303-505-0866 to arrange a repair assessment.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
